WEBVTT

00:01:28.920 --> 00:01:32.076
When we become infected,
or we have disease,

00:01:32.100 --> 00:01:35.776
typically, we try to sleep longer,
we stay in bed longer.

00:01:35.800 --> 00:01:36.958
So in other words,

00:01:36.982 --> 00:01:41.501
it was the unmeasured disease
and sickness in those studies

00:01:41.525 --> 00:01:45.231
that was triggering
a response in those individuals

00:01:45.255 --> 00:01:46.791
to try and sleep more.

00:01:46.815 --> 00:01:48.081
That's one explanation.

00:01:48.105 --> 00:01:52.201
The second possible explanation
is poor sleep quality,

00:01:52.225 --> 00:01:54.881
because we know that sleep quality,

00:01:54.905 --> 00:01:58.301
independent of sleep quantity,

00:01:58.325 --> 00:02:01.831
is also associated with mortality risk.